// A61: a designated list as an argument is reported as an ineligible struct instead of a
// missing destination type.
// Diagnostic quality: a designated list in argument position. The message
// claims the struct is ineligible ("requires a struct with public value
// fields, no declared constructors, and no inheritance ...") although Point
// satisfies every listed condition; the real issue is the missing
// destination type (static-semantics.md:370-379 only defines it for a
// declared destination).
import std.vector;
struct Point {
  int x;
  int y;
};
int main() {
  mut std::vector<Point> points{};
  points.push_back({.x = 1, .y = 2});
  return int(points.size());
}
